messages:
maria: Hey team — hitting weird drops with our Go client streaming when auth refresh kicks in. Anyone seen http2/context + auth-refresh weirdness? Asking before I dive deep.

ajay: Are these gRPC streams or raw HTTP/2 streaming? behaviour differs a lot.

maria: Raw HTTP/2 streaming (server-sent chunks). We use http.Client + custom RoundTripper that injects Authorization and does a sync refresh+retry on 401. Problem: when refresh happens mid-stream, server cancels and client sees EOF. Looks like the stream is torn down when the RT does the retry. Pasting simplified RT flow below.

lina: If your RoundTripper blocks to refresh and then effectively issues a new request on the same logical call, http2 will close the original stream. Can you paste the RT snippet?

maria: ````go
// simplified pseudocode
func (rt *authRT) RoundTrip(req *http.Request) (*http.Response, error) {
  // inject token
  req2 := req.Clone(req.Context())
  req2.Header.Set("Authorization", "Bearer "+rt.token.Value)
  resp, err := rt.base.RoundTrip(req2)
  if err != nil { return nil, err }
  if resp.StatusCode == 401 {
    // refresh token synchronously
    rt.refresh()
    // retry — but body is io.ReadCloser and already consumed for streaming requests
    return rt.base.RoundTrip(req2)
  }
  return resp, nil
}
````

jen: A few concrete tips:
1) You must be able to re-create the request body for retries (use req.GetBody or buffer to []byte; streaming bodies can't be retried unless rewindable).
2) When retrying, use a fresh *http.Request created with req.Clone(ctx) instead of reusing the same object across streams.
3) Avoid actions that replace the Transport or call CloseIdleConnections while an active stream is in-flight — that will tear down streams.

sam: Also check your Transport config: set MaxIdleConnsPerHost to a high value, IdleConnTimeout to something reasonable, and do NOT set DisableKeepAlives=true for streaming. Example:
````go
tr := &http.Transport{
  ForceAttemptHTTP2:     true,
  MaxIdleConnsPerHost:   128,
  IdleConnTimeout:       90 * time.Second,
}
client := &http.Client{Transport: tr, Timeout: 0} // no global timeout for streaming
````

ci-bot: FYI: our CI uses http2 by default for the runtime client tests.

lina: For context propagation: ensure you create the request with the intended ctx (req = req.WithContext(ctx) or req.Clone(ctx)) before the RoundTripper path. If you need to retry, clone again with the same ctx. Don't try to swap in a new ctx on the response-reading goroutine — propagate it when creating requests.

ajay: About keepalive/pings: the Go stdlib client doesn't expose a client-side http2 PingInterval. If you're fighting idle drops you can: increase IdleConnTimeout, implement application-level pings over the stream, or use lower-level golang.org/x/net/http2 Transport/ConfigureTransport if you need more control. The server side should also be tuned (read_idle, ping intervals).

maria: One observed issue — when context is canceled, some goroutines block on resp.Body.Read even after ctx.Done. Is resp.Body.Close() the recommended pattern?

lina: Yes. On ctx cancel you should Close the body to unblock readers. Pattern: read loop should select on ctx.Done() and call resp.Body.Close().
Example:````go
buf := make([]byte, 4096)
for {
  select {
  case <-ctx.Done():
    resp.Body.Close()
    return ctx.Err()
  default:
    n, err := resp.Body.Read(buf)
    if err != nil { return err }
    // process buf[:n]
  }
}
````

jen: Bonus: for token refresh you might prefer a non-blocking refresher that pre-warms tokens or refreshes on a timer so you avoid in-flight synchronous refreshes that cause stream restarts. Also provide req.GetBody on requests that may be retried.

sam: And do NOT call Transport.CloseIdleConnections as a retry strategy — that will close active http2 streams.

maria: Great tips. I'll: 1) update RT to clone req and buffer small bodies with GetBody; 2) avoid CloseIdleConnections; 3) ensure resp.Body.Close on ctx cancel; 4) bump MaxIdleConnsPerHost.

maria: If these don't fix it I'll post logs and a minimal repro. Thanks all :thumbsup:

ci-bot: CI: client/runtime tests on branch fix/rt-retry — all green :white_check_mark:
